		1601 -> 1934;
	1602 [label="I hope someday you can meet him.",shape=box,color=red];
		1602 -> 1609;
	1614 [label="Merci ! À la revoyure !",shape=box,color=blue];
		1614 -> 1617;
	1615 [label="Oh ! It is one of the Rights of Lua. On the anniversary of the passing of a soul, one braids a crown or wreath flowers and places it atop their skull or atop their grave. ",shape=box,color=blue];
		1615 -> 1618;
	1616 [label="Merci, I will ! À la revoyure !",shape=box,color=blue];
		1616 -> 1617;
	1609 [label="Oui. But it is not his silence that troubles me, I suppose. I asked Monsieur Necraloid if the skull that adorned him belonged to a living soul at one point or another or not.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1609 -> 1936;
	1617 [label="Chat ends.",color=orange];
	1618 [label="Traditional crypts for the dead often had the bodies exposed, oui ? So you could do this. I think some of this survived, even still.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1618 -> 1619;
	1619 [label="I see it reflected in some of the Orokin artwork, with their love of skulls. ",shape=box,color=blue];
		1619 -> 1620;
		1619 -> 1621;
		1619 -> 1622;
	1620 [label="That does explain a lot.",shape=box,color=red];
		1620 -> 1623;
	1621 [label="The more things change, huh?",shape=box,color=red];
		1621 -> 1623;
	1622 [label="I think Daughter has tried to do that before, you'll make her jealous.",shape=box,color=red];
		1622 -> 1624;
	1623 [label="Oui ! So much time has passed, and yet the influence remains. It brings me happiness to know even tiny pieces remain.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1623 -> 1625;
	1624 [label="Oui ? Then I look forward to the day I can meet her ! I will tell her I gave him no quarter.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1624 -> 1625;
	1625 [label="Faux skull or no, Monsieur Necraloid should have a crown. And it makes him so shy when I dote upon him ! He would blush if he could, I think. And this makes me smile.",shape=box,color=blue];
		1625 -> 1626;
	1626 [label="À la revoyure !",shape=box,color=blue];
		1626 -> 1627;
